            "arabic_text": "يُونُسُ عَنْ أَبَانِ بْنِ تَغْلِبَ عَمَّنْ رَوَاهُ عَنْ أَبِي عَبْدِ اللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ السَّلَامُ قَالَ:",
            "chunk_type": "isnad",
            "translations": {
              "bn": "",
              "de": "",
              "en": "Yūnus, from Abān ibn Taghlib, from one who narrated it, from Abī ʿAbdillāh عليه السلام, who said:",
              "es": "",
              "fa": "",
              "fr": "",
              "id": "",
              "ru": "",
              "tr": "",
              "ur": "",
              "zh": ""
            },
            "word_end": 14,
            "word_start": 0
          },
          {
            "arabic_text": "«إِذَا قَتَلَ الْعَبْدُ الْحُرَّ دُفِعَ إِلَى أَوْلِيَاءِ الْمَقْتُولِ، فَإِنْ شَاءُوا قَتَلُوهُ، وَإِنْ شَاءُوا حَبَسُوهُ يَكُونُ عَبْدًا لَهُمْ، وَإِنْ شَاءُوا اسْتَرَقُّوهُ».",
            "chunk_type": "body",
            "translations": {
              "bn": "",
              "de": "",
              "en": "“When a slave kills a free man, he is handed over to the heirs of the slain person. If they wish, they may kill him; if they wish, they may detain him so that he becomes a slave belonging to them; and if they wish, they may enslave him.”",
              "es": "",
              "fa": "",
              "fr": "",
              "id": "",
              "ru": "",
              "tr": "",
              "ur": "",
              "zh": ""
            },
